WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:06.160
David, I hear often that the country is more
divided than ever, but it's divided for a

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.200
good reason.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.910
One side is insane.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.940
Is it really that bad for the country to be
divided?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.720
I think it's important to, to answer this
question, to understand that partisanship

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.640
and division are two different things, and
I'm not saying the country isn't divided,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:28.970
but divided might point more towards the types
of circumstances that would lead to a civil

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:29.970
war.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:30.970
Right?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.719
We're half the country wants to separate the
South wants to succeed in order to maintain

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:39.920
state's rights, to have slavery be illegal,
for example.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.130
We don't have that level of division right
now.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.059
There are some secessionists but not that
many.

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:48.590
A lot of us who say, Hey, if the red States
want to bail, go ahead.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.609
We are the financially viable blue States.

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:51.609
We're sort of joking.

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:55.090
I mean it would be extraordinarily damaging
to the country if the country were to separate

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.730
into financially.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.039
Even if mathematically in the long run the
blue States would be fine and the red States

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:04.879
wouldn't, um, it would be such a jolt to the
system that it would be very bad for the economy.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:11.660
For, for a while the partisanship we are seeing
is partially because we are sort of coming

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:19.130
to a potentially big change in the path of
America and I don't want to excuse the partisanship

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:24.290
as merely sensible because of this precipice
we might be approaching.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:29.700
Part of the reason we have this partisanship
is because of partisan media, including the

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.490
existence of Fox news and other right wing
media, a carrying water in a way that doesn't

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.890
relate to the facts on the ground at all.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.329
Social media echo chambers.

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:42.350
Like there are some really toxic reasons why
we have such partisanship that even though

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.970
the country has moved to the left, a lot of
money is still raised by the right by kind

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:52.250
of hunkering down these extremist reactionary
positions on abortion and immigrants and so

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.250
on and so forth.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:58.640
So there's a lot of really horrible reasons
why we have partisanship, but also our system

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.850
rewards partisanship.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:05.770
If you run centrists campaigns, it becomes
harder to raise money for reelection because

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.600
you're not appealing to the people who are
most um, radical.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.490
And I use that term non-judgmentally when
it comes to issues.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.840
Radical positions justify and encourage more
donations.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.410
And that's part of the system that we have.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.600
But to some degree, the election of Donald
Trump was insane.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:29.660
And now there is a question, are, are we reelecting
Trump and saying Trump was not an anomaly

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.540
or an anomaly, depending on which pronunciation
you like, we are, we've had four years of

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.580
Trump and we're going to four more.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.000
That would be a huge thing for the country
to do.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.310
On the other hand, we have the possibility
of electing the most progressive presidents

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.030
in the history of the United States.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.170
Bernie Sanders or Elizabeth Warren, uh, even
some of the other candidates would be more

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.440
progressive than anyone else who has been
president so far.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.520
So I believe that the hyper partisanship in
part is also because of this precipice of

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.220
possible significant change that we're going
to have the media fomented the media profits

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.350
from it, no question about it.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.740
And we are living in two different realities.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.240
Media foments that in part the internet is
a huge part of it.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.350
You have everything from militant conspiracy
theorists, more and more white supremacy far

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.490
right, hyper nationalist types.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:24.630
There is increasingly a lack of middle ground
represented in media.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:28.640
Social media reinforces more and more extreme
versions of whatever it is that you believe

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.740
or support and it's extraordinarily powerful.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:38.440
Getting through to people and saying, let's
be sensible becomes difficult and often not

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.440
rewarded.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.680
When, when you look at polls about what TV
shows, what podcasts, what websites the left

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.760
and the right are looking at, they are very
different and they are increasingly ones that

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.680
merely reinforce and continue to radicalize
that preexisting worldview.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.630
So serious division has many negative effects.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:04.140
Both sides can be more easily controlled by
a minority of their side, uh, by picking the

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.400
issues that will most catalyze and rational
and a reaction.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:17.010
Air create views and that can be done in perpetuity
to keep increasing the division or partisanship.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.520
Uh, the deepening political divide can also
lead to violence.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:26.610
We've talked about how many of us believe
if Donald Trump were to be, uh, um, removed

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:33.080
from office by losing in 2020, but claim that
it was unfair that it was rigged in some way.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:38.430
I fear that there would be violence and uh,
hyper partisanship and division can also cause

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:44.500
that, but I don't believe the country is so
much divided as it is hyper-partisan which

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.960
comes with its own set of issues.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.470
What do you think is the country divided?

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:51.750
Hyper-partisan a little bit of both.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.750
One or the other.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.090
I want to hear from you

